---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Laptop, Monitor, Keyboard, Mouse, Headphones } from 'lucide-astro';
---
<Base title="Uses" description="Tools I use for building products, writing code, and keeping the work moving.">

  <div class="page-heading">
    <h1>Uses</h1>
    <p>The tools I reach for every day, plus a few opinions earned by using them.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="tools-section">
    <p class="section-label">Things that power my life</p>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/claude-color.svg" alt="Claude" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Claude</span>
        <p>Still my first choice for frontend work. It tends to understand the visual intent without sanding off all the personality.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/codex-color.svg" alt="Codex" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Codex</span>
        <p>My broad engineering workhorse — useful for exploring a codebase, planning changes, and carrying the implementation through.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/cursor.svg" alt="Cursor" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Cursor</span>
        <p>The editor I use most. I still keep VS Code nearby, but Cursor's integrated workflow usually wins me back.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/opencode-light.svg" alt="OpenCode" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">OpenCode</span>
        <p>One of the best interfaces I've tried for AI-assisted coding: focused, fast, and pleasantly out of the way.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/ghostty.svg" alt="Ghostty" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Ghostty</span>
        <p>Terminal that's fast, native, and actually pleasant to look at.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/notion.svg" alt="Notion" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Notion</span>
        <p>I keep trying alternatives. Its flexibility keeps pulling me back, which is probably the strongest endorsement I can give it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="tools-section">
    <p class="section-label">Things that power my apps</p>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/nextjs.svg" alt="Next.js" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Next.js</span>
        <p>Familiar, productive, and rarely the part of a project I need to think about. That's usually enough.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/astro.svg" alt="Astro" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Astro</span>
        <p>Used it for this very site. Ships zero JS by default, which is the only correct default.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/expo-icon-2.svg" alt="Expo" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Expo</span>
        <p>How I build mobile apps. I haven't touched a native Android or iOS bundle in years and I'd like to keep it that way.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/convex.svg" alt="Convex" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Convex</span>
        <p>Less boilerplate. Real-time built in. Still not sure how it works under the hood and I've made peace with that.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/stripe (1).svg" alt="Stripe" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Stripe</span>
        <p>The docs are good. That's it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/posthog.svg" alt="PostHog" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">PostHog</span>
        <p>Tells you what your users are actually doing, not what you think they're doing. Humbling.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  {/* Hidden for now — "Things on my desk" section
  <div class="tools-section">
    <p class="section-label">Things on my desk</p>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon"><Laptop size={22} /></div>
